## Vue 3 Revolution

The Composition API is a new way to organize Vue components, offering superior flexibility to the Options API.

## Reactivity Basics

```javascript
import { ref, reactive, computed } from 'vue'

const count = ref(0)
const state = reactive({
  user: {
    name: 'John'
  }
})

const doubled = computed(() => count.value * 2)
```

## Setup Function

The `<script setup>` simplifies the syntax:

```vue
<script setup>
import { ref } from 'vue'

const count = ref(0)
const increment = () => {
  count.value++
}
</script>
```

## Composables

Extract reusable logic into composables:

```javascript
export function useCounter() {
  const count = ref(0)
  const increment = () => count.value++

  return { count, increment }
}
```

## Lifecycle

Lifecycle hooks work within setup:

```javascript
import { onMounted, onUnmounted } from 'vue'

onMounted(() => {
  console.log('Component mounted')
})

onUnmounted(() => {
  console.log('Component destroyed')
})
```

## Conclusion

The Composition API offers power, flexibility and better code organization.

